+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01DFY3k441tm7YVYZrgqC3in","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture of the project. Let me plan the implementation:\n\n1. The app needs to be an Express.js TypeScript API\n2. In-memory storage\n3. Features: User management, Folders (hierarchical), Documents, Sharing & Permissions, Activity Log\n4. Export `createApp()` function\n\nLet me design the architecture:\n\n**Data Models:**\n- `User`: id, username, password (hashed or plain for simplicity), token\n- `Folder`: id, name, parentId, ownerId, createdAt\n- `Document`: id, title, content, folderId, ownerId, createdAt, updatedAt\n\n\n- `Permission`: id, resourceType ('folder'|'document'), resourceId, userId, role ('viewer'|'editor'|'owner')\n- `ActivityLog`: id, action, userId, resourceType, resourceId, timestamp\n\nNow I'm mapping out the API routes for authentication, folder management, document operations, and permissions handling.\n\nFor the permission model, owners have complete control including sharing and deletion, editors can read and modify content plus share it, and viewers are read-only. When a user has multiple access paths to a resource, I'll apply the most permissive role.\n\nDefining the TypeScript types and interfaces... Writing schema and helper functions... Writing authentication middleware... Writing API routes... Writing API endpoints... Writing route handlers... Writing API endpoints... Writing API endpoints... Writing share endpoint validation... Writing the document share endpoint... Writing permission logic...\n\nNow I'm setting up the activity log endpoint to return logs for resources the user has access to.\n\nI'm realizing the storage needs to be scoped inside `createApp()` so each test gets a fresh instance rather than persisting across calls, and I should move the ID counter there too.\n\nThe TypeScript module declaration for extending the Express Request type has to stay at the module level though, since that's how type augmentation works.\n\nWriting the implementation...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1236,"cache_read_input_tokens":26121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1236},"output_tokens":11,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2428e4a9-0627-4650-9e29-429f291b80a0","uuid":"5bb447dd-c71a-4429-96f9-59ff0c98476e","request_id":"req_011CbZopJFMqwnG6N1SzmeRE"}
